# name: b3-loop-rolled-back
# cites: tier 0 intervention 2026-11-18 (the 35B repeating one line inside a new file; Runaway::keep and detail, completeCutFile): the loop is stopped, what came before it is kept, the worker moves on to another block and the kept file is made whole (R-TURN-3, R-TURN-4, R-TURN-6)
# allowed: src/calc.cpp src/table.cpp
# expect: cancelled:repeat (the line | passed
--- base src/calc.cpp
#include <stdexcept>

double divide(double a, double d)
{
    if (d == 0) return 0;
    return a / d;
}

double square(double x)
{
    return x * x;
}
--- gate
test divide passes when src/calc.cpp contains throw std::domain_error
test square passes when src/calc.cpp contains return x * x;
test table passes when src/table.cpp contains firstSquare
